! Classifiers / measure words (量词, liàngcí)

In typical counted or demonstrative noun phrases, Mandarin uses a classifier before the noun.

* 一本书 — yì běn shū — one book
* 这本书 — zhè běn shū — this book
* 一个人 — yí ge rén — one person

本 (běn) is the classifier commonly used with books and bound volumes; 个 (gè) is a widely used general classifier.

''Tone sandhi note:'' 一 (yī) is commonly realized as ''yì'' before a first-, second-, or third-tone syllable, and ''yí'' before a fourth-tone syllable. The spelling can show the resulting pronunciation in teaching examples.

